WEBVTT

00:00:00.180 --> 00:00:04.384
Maya wants to improve her school garden.
Before she can

00:00:04.384 --> 00:00:08.588
redesign it, she needs permission and a
spot with suitable

00:00:08.588 --> 00:00:09.008
light.

00:00:09.380 --> 00:00:13.731
First ask a staff sponsor about
permission. Next sketch one

00:00:13.731 --> 00:00:18.082
possible bed and note the sunlight. Then
review the plan

00:00:18.082 --> 00:00:21.562
with the sponsor and decide whether to
continue.

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:26.253
Maya can sketch and observe without
planting. If she cannot

00:00:26.253 --> 00:00:30.526
visit the site safely, she can document
that barrier and

00:00:30.526 --> 00:00:33.518
ask what information the sponsor can
share.

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.874
A dated sketch or a short note about the
sunlight

00:00:37.874 --> 00:00:41.767
could help compare locations. One
observation cannot prove that a

00:00:41.767 --> 00:00:44.493
garden will thrive across a whole
season.

00:00:44.980 --> 00:00:49.415
Feedback might lead Maya to choose
another spot or gather

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:53.851
more evidence. For your project, name
one safe action, one

00:00:53.851 --> 00:00:57.843
useful observation, and one thing it
would not prove.

